{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And Abraham and Sarah were old.</b> What does this tell me? Further on it says 'and Abraham was old, come into days.' Rather, it teaches that HaShem restored him to youthfulness, and it was necessary to write a second time 'and Abraham was old.' Bereshit Rabbah." "<b>Old, come into days.</b> From the beginning of the book until here, you will not find old age written about any person, until Abraham came and said before HaShem: Master of the universe, a man and his son enter the same place and no one knows whom to honor; but since You adorn him with white hair, one knows whom to honor. HaShem said to him: a good thing you have requested, and from you it begins. From the beginning of the book until Isaac — suffering is not written, until Isaac came and requested suffering. He said before Him: Master of the universe, a man who dies without suffering — the measure of justice is stretched out against him. HaShem said to him: by your life, a good thing you have requested, and from you it begins: 'and his eyes were dim from seeing.' Jacob requested illness. He said: Master of the universe, a man who dies without illness does not settle his affairs among his sons, but since he is ill two or three days, he settles his affairs among his sons. HaShem said to him: by your life, a good thing you have requested, and from you it begins. As it is written: 'and he said to Joseph, behold your father is ill.' Thus Abraham introduced old age, as it says 'and Abraham was old.' Isaac introduced suffering, as it says 'and it was when Isaac was old and his eyes were dim from seeing.' Jacob introduced illness, as it is written 'behold your father is ill.'" "<b>Ceased to be for Sarah the way of women.</b> Other old women do not have a menstrual cycle, and this one was old and saw a menstrual flow, as Rashi explained regarding 'and he took butter and milk.'"], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {0 "The abbreviation ת״ל is resolved as מה ת״‎ל 'what does it tell me/teach,' a standard Chizkuni marker."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:04:44.488324003Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}